{"id":111388520470819,"type":"album","name":"Jurassic Shift","artist":"Ozric Tentacles","year":1993,"weight":23,"info":{"cover":"https://dn721900.ca.archive.org/0/items/mbid-b60ce7da-e361-49f6-a742-1867a0612762/mbid-b60ce7da-e361-49f6-a742-1867a0612762-35772621734.jpg","kind":"Album","tracks":8,"country":"US","scaruffi":7.0,"sputnik":4.16,"yt":"KAVzL4Q6lRw","links":{"spotify":"https://open.spotify.com/album/1sBTE8pk2bYgcqI3C0xBnw","youtube":"https://music.youtube.com/playlist?list=OLAK5uy_nkwBAUk8BXY8MS2HKHo5_c-3PmR9CZKmI","bandcamp":"https://kscopemusic.bandcamp.com/album/jurassic-shift-2020-ed-wynne-remaster","rateyourmusic":"https://rateyourmusic.com/release/album/ozric-tentacles/jurassic-shift","sputnikmusic":"https://www.sputnikmusic.com/album/30229/Ozric-Tentacles-Jurassic-Shift/"},"desc":"The music style of this album is very hard to categorize: it is a brilliant mix of progressive space rock, hard rock, fusion, techno, New Age with TONS of state-of-the-art keyboards. ALL the instruments steal the show. The VERY varied, atmospheric, weird and colorful keyboards, combined with the incisive hard rock guitar a la Steve Hillage create absolutely \"out of this world\" dynamic spacescapes. Easily comparable to the Gong space-era stuff, \"Jurassic Shift\" however has more crystal clear textures with ultra modern keyboards. The drums and bass are NEVER bland nor repetitive; they are VERY elaborated and clearly contribute to ."},"artist_ref":{"id":193248221396770,"name":"Ozric Tentacles","info":{"img":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Ozric_Tentacles_live_in_Zagreb_in_2004.jpg?width=500"}},"labels":[],"genres":[{"id":185670346256268,"type":"genre","name":"rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":3782,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":87625349211221,"type":"genre","name":"electronic","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":1332,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":262736572970899,"type":"genre","name":"Space Rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":282,"yt":